9. **The after reads** (after the child, before the teardown): the same reads as step 7, and these words:
   - `ledger-after`, `bin-after`, `bin-new` (the count of `bin/` names not in `bin-before`), `cwd-verify-after`;
   - `claude-json-keys`: `same`, or `+<added>` / `-<removed>` top-level key names;
   - `projects-new`: the count of `projects` keys present after and not before (the run's own entries, matched by
     their paths in memory, never by the shared file's hash: host-linux 2026-11-17);
   - `projects-new-keys`: the sorted union of the key NAMES inside those new entries;
   - `disabled-mcp`: `written` when a new entry whose key lies under `<cwd>/.viola-verify-` holds `disabledMcpServers`,
     `none` when such entries exist and none holds it, `unread` when no such entry was found or the file was not read
     (Run B's own project entry, `inputs#I2` item 1's `/mcp disable` reading; RED on `unread`, `founder-forks.md` (c));
   - `needle-claude-json` and `needle-settings`: `<before>/<after>` words;
   - `settings-keys`: `same`, or the per-file key-name delta, file names only;
   - `stamp-others`: `kept` when every non-2.1.325 entry is value-equal before and after, `changed` otherwise,
     `unread` on a failed read.

11. **`crates/viola-e2e/src/rig/isolate.rs`** — the helpers, each pure or bounded through `MAX_FRAME`, none printing:
    - `child_env_real(cli_dir, run)`: `child_env` without `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` (the kept host names, `cli_dir` first on
      `PATH`, `TERM`, the run marker);
    - `entry_names(dir) -> Option<Vec<String>>`; `key_names(path) -> Option<BTreeSet<String>>` (top level);
      `project_entries(path) -> Option<BTreeMap<String, BTreeSet<String>>>`; `needle_word(path, needle)`;
      `key_delta(before, after) -> String`; `others_word(before, after, version) -> &'static str`.

12. **Unit cases, inline** (labelled `(label, …)` case tables, viola-e2e carries no rstest; tests S1, S3, S4):
    - labels: `L1`, `L1-2` → `VH`; `L2` → `CX`; `L1-3`, `L2-2` → `None`; `parse("vh")`, `parse("cx")`; the `VH` and
      `CX` property rows;
    - `child_env_real` holds no `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, holds the marker, and leads `PATH` with `cli_dir`;
    - `key_delta`: same → `same`; one added and one removed → both named;
    - `project_entries` / the `disabled-mcp` reading over planted configs: a new `.viola-verify-` entry holding
      `disabledMcpServers` → `written`; holding other keys → `none`; no new entry → `unread`;
    - `needle_word`: present, absent, an unreadable path → `unread`;
    - `others_word` over in-memory documents: kept, one other version changed → `changed`, an absent file → `unread`
      (no stamps file is hand-written: tests · decision/stamps-written-only-by-verify).

14. **`arm_cx`**, R2's shape (`mod.rs:1680-1752`) with one text:
    - the first frame must be the box with no trust form, else `refused: shape`; `session-start` awaited and the
      session id learned;
    - one `viola --home <vhome> send rig-cx --json --file <texts>/1.txt`, the file holding `/context`, bounded by
      `SEND_BOUND`: `send-1-reply` = `send_word` (`ok` or `<refusal>:<detail>`, closed code words);
    - before the send, the session's transcript `<scratch config>/projects/*/<session id>.jsonl` (one level, found
      by the learned id) is located and its length kept; `context-transcript`: `read` · `absent` · `unread`;
    - for `SUBMIT_BOUND`: `context-submitted` = `yes` when a `prompt-submitted` whose text equals `/context` arrives,
      else `no`; `context-tags` = the count of `<local-command-stdout>` openings past the kept length (through
      `MAX_FRAME`, no byte kept);
    - `context-post`: `both` · `prompt-submitted` · `tag` · `none`;
    - then the rig's own stop (Ctrl-C into its own pty; `inputs#I2` item 9). The rig grants no key.

- **Research files inspected** (research rev 1), and read at P4:
  - `crates/viola-e2e/src/rig/mod.rs:1-535` (arms, `start`, `finish`), `:751-891` (`run_child`, `end_session`),
    `:1187-1210` (`arm_v`), `:1584-1752` (`new_lines`, `await_kind`, `send_word`, `arm_r2`);
  - `crates/viola-e2e/src/rig/isolate.rs:1-240` (`TOKEN_FLOOR`, `stamp`, `witness`, `child_env`, `Scratch::create`);
  - `crates/viola-e2e/src/bin/viola-live-rig.rs:90-232`;
  - `crates/viola-e2e/tests/rig_rehearsal.rs` (case list, `:1035-1110` the `vp` rehearsal);
  - `src/cmd/verify.rs:225-315`; `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/ledger.rs:1103-1131`;
  - `tests/cli_verify.rs:640-715, 850-895`; `tests/cli_send.rs:1220-1270`; `tests/support/verify.rs:43-49, 481-643`;
  - `scripts/release-check.sh`; `.config/nextest.toml:9-55` (the `verify_window_` override);
  - `~/.viola/bin/` and `~/.viola/ledger/` by name (three keys; `probes`, `stamps.json`, `stamps.json.lock`).

9. **The after reads** (after the child, before the teardown): the same reads as step 7, and these words:
   - `ledger-after`, `bin-after`, `bin-new` (the count of `bin/` names not in `bin-before`), `cwd-verify-after`;
   - `claude-json-keys`: `same`, or `+<added>` / `-<removed>` top-level key names;
   - `projects-new`: the count of `projects` keys present after and not before (the run's own entries, matched by
     their paths in memory, never by the shared file's hash: host-linux 2026-11-17);
   - `projects-new-keys`: the sorted union of the key NAMES inside those new entries;
   - `disabled-mcp`: `written` when a new entry whose key lies under `<cwd>/.viola-verify-` holds `disabledMcpServers`,
     `none` when such entries exist and none holds it, `unread` when no such entry was found or the file was not read
     (Run B's own project entry, `inputs#I2` item 1's `/mcp disable` reading; RED on `unread`, `founder-forks.md` (c));
   - `needle-claude-json` and `needle-settings`: `<before>/<after>` words;
   - `settings-keys`: `same`, or the per-file key-name delta, file names only;
   - `stamp-others`: `kept` when every entry other than `plan.cli_version`'s (2.1.325 among them) is value-equal before and after, `changed` otherwise,
     `unread` on a failed read.

- **Read:** the closure's reads, by byte search with no start (`command grep -ao … | wc -l` for counts, `command grep -aob -m1` for first offsets), each on `~/.local/share/mise/installs/claude/2.1.325/claude` and `…/2.1.328/claude`:
  - `claudeInChromeDefaultEnabled` — 25 occurrences on 2.1.325 (first byte 154 780 724), 24 on 2.1.328 (first byte 154 803 008): holds (the prompt's handler writes it on either answer, the offer is skipped while it is defined; the one fewer reader is an auto-connect check);
  - `Yes, use my browser` — 2 lines each (2.1.325 byte 168 565 712; 2.1.328 byte 168 801 412), beside `Claude in Chrome extension detected` (168 565 776; 168 801 476): holds;
  - `hasTrustDialogAccepted` — 22 occurrences each (first bytes 154 781 140; 154 803 424): holds;
  - `disabledMcpServers` — 9 occurrences each (first bytes 157 411 852; 157 522 384): holds; whether an absent server name reaches the writer stays unmeasured;
  - `AddedFolderTrustPrompt` — 0 on 2.1.325, 4 on 2.1.328: new, reached only through `--add-dir`, which no viola spawn passes (`grep -rn add-dir src crates`: none) — outside the plan's surfaces;
  - the rig's seeded markers (`crates/viola-e2e/src/rig/isolate.rs:537-553`): the migration constant 15 on both bundles, the other names with equal counts (revision run `2026-11-19T06-05-00Z-phase`);
  - `~/.viola/ledger/stamps.json` by `jq`: the 2.1.328 entry 21 rows all `pass`, `verified_at` 2026-11-19T06:03:11Z; 2.1.325 at 21 rows (revision run `2026-11-19T06-05-00Z-phase`); `~/.viola/bin/` three keys by name;
  - the tree: `git diff --stat HEAD -- src crates tests` empty (the stopped run edited nothing); `df -h /home` 287G free; `target/` 13G, `target/release/viola` built 2026-11-19T06:09:52Z by the revision-1 window (its duration not kept).

9. **The after reads** (after the child, before the teardown): the same reads as step 7, and these words:
   - `ledger-after`, `bin-after`, `bin-new` (the count of `bin/` names not in `bin-before`), `cwd-verify-after`;
   - `claude-json-keys`: `same`, or `+<added>` / `-<removed>` top-level key names;
   - `projects-new`: the count of `projects` keys present after and not before (the run's own entries, matched by
     their paths in memory, never by the shared file's hash: host-linux 2026-11-17);
   - `projects-new-keys`: the sorted union of the key NAMES inside those new entries;
   - `disabled-mcp`: `written` when a new entry whose key lies under `<cwd>/.viola-verify-` holds `disabledMcpServers`,
     `none` when such entries exist and none holds it, `unread` when no such entry was found or the file was not read
     (Run B's own project entry, `inputs#I2` item 1's `/mcp disable` reading). Revision 3 (`inputs#I15` item 3):
     `unread` is no longer RED. It stays the rig's honest word for «no entry to read it from», and the needle words
     carry the reading;
   - `needle-claude-json` and `needle-settings`: `<before>/<after>` words;
   - `settings-keys`: `same`, or the per-file key-name delta, file names only;
   - `stamp-others`: `kept` when every entry other than `plan.cli_version`'s (2.1.325 among them) is value-equal before and after, `changed` otherwise,
     `unread` on a failed read.

- **Revision 3, the mended expect's failing readings** (`inputs#I16` item 1). Each of these turns entry 14 red:
  - `needle-claude-json` or `needle-settings` reading `unread` on its before side (`lacks needle-…: unread`);
  - either word reading `unread` on its after side (`lacks needle-…: absent/unread` and `…: present/unread`);
  - either word moving `absent` → `present` (`lacks needle-…: absent/present`);
  - either word missing from the summary (`contains needle-…:`).

  The `{before}/{after}` form is `rig/mod.rs`'s `put_after` (`format!("{}/{}", …)`), and each half is `needle_word`'s
  `present` · `absent` · `unread` (`rig/isolate.rs`). So these atoms cover every unread and every absent → present
  pair. A needle `present` on both sides stood before the start, and it does not fail the entry.

- Run `2026-11-19T06-21-00Z-implement`, Bash guard refusals:
  - a heredoc to a file target was refused; the edits went through the Edit tool;
  - a recursive rm of `$TMPDIR/vrig-hand-7IXWRN` was refused; the dir stands, on the desk list.

- **Outcome basis:** this run (`2026-11-19T07-06-34Z-implement`), plus the earlier runs' outcome files, each read:
  - `2026-11-19T06-14-06Z-implement` (stuck, on 2.1.325 vs 2.1.328; absorbed by revision 1);
  - `2026-11-19T06-21-00Z-implement` (stuck, on the R1 count; absorbed by revision 2; its code and deviations
    carried);
  - `2026-11-19T06-49-43Z-implement` (stuck, on `L1`'s atom; absorbed by revision 3; its `L1` reading carried).

